<template>
    <p>
        This document is the reference API for every component shipped with the Phue
        frontend toolkit (`PhUI`).<br>Components live in `src/Core/UI/Phui/*.phue` and are
        single-file <strong>Vue 3</strong> modules styled with <strong>Bootstrap 5</strong> utility classes.<br> There is no
        build step, no npm (excluded the ph-code component), and no component whitelist to maintain.
    </p>
    <ph-card>
        <template #header>
            <h4><strong>How components are used</strong></h4>
        </template>
        <template #default>
            <h5 class="fw-bold">No imports, no registration</h5>
            <p>
                Pages are .phue templates. When the framework compiles a page it scans the template
                with PhueComponentLoader (src/Core/UI/ComponentDiscoverer.php) and auto-imports every
                component the template actually references — and only those: <strong>no whitelist, no import;</strong>
                auto-discovered from the template and imported into one self-sufficient module, minted per page.
            </p>
            <p>You just write the tag in kebab-case:</p>
            <ph-code
                language="vue"
                :code="snippet1_1"
                maxHeight="450px"
                :themeSwitcher="false"
                class="mb-3"
            />
            <p>The loader builds the <code class="mx-1"> components: { PhButton, PhInput, ... }</code> map itself and only ships the JS module for the referenced components.</p>
            <!-- 1.1.1 -->
            <p class="fw-bold">Component Styles Metadata ('styles' in {{'<php>'}} block)</p>
            <p>A .phue component (page or partial) can declare its own stylesheet dependencies in the <code>{{'<php>'}}</code> block return array:</p>
            <ph-code
                language="phue"
                :code="snippet1_1_1"
                maxHeight="450px"
                :themeSwitcher="false"
                class="mb-3"
            />

            <strong>Flow:</strong>
            <ol>
                <li><p>Component's <code>{{'<php>'}}</code> block returns 'styles' => [...] (array of URLs)</p></li>
                <li><p><code>PhueComponentLoader</code> passes it to View constructor ($styles param)</p></li>
                <li><p><code>ComponentRenderer::renderView()</code> iterates $view->getStyles() and calls $assetRegistry->addRequestStyle($url) for each</p></li>
                <li><p><code>HtmlShellRenderer</code> renders {{'<link rel="stylesheet" href="...">'}} in {{'<head>'}}</p></li>
                <li><p><code>AssetRegistry::beginRequest()</code> clears the request pool — styles are request-scoped, no leak across pages</p></li>
            </ol>

            <p class="text-muted">
                <strong>Key point:</strong> Styles are <strong>request-scoped</strong> (lazy).
                Each page/component declares its own styles, they're added to the request pool
                during render, and cleared on the next <code>beginRequest()</code>. No global pollution,
                no manual cleanup needed.
            </p>
            <p class="text-muted">
                <strong>BC note:</strong> <code>$styles</code> was appended as the last <code>View</code> constructor parameter
                (after $html), so existing positional calls <code>new View($tpl, $state, $scripts, $inlineScript, $html)</code>
                remain 100% compatible.
            </p>
            <p class="text-muted">
                <strong>Asset URL convention:</strong> Use absolute paths from registered asset sources,
                e.g. <code>/assets/app/styles/main.css</code> (serves <code>App/Assets/styles/main.css</code> via <code>registerSource('/assets/app', ...)</code>
                in <code>public/index.php</code>.
            </p>

            <ph-card class="mb-3">
                <h5 class="fw-bold">v-model is wired per component</h5>
                <ph-data-table
                    :columns="[
                        {key: 'form', label: 'Form'},
                        {key: 'props_updated', label: 'Props Updated'},
                        {key: 'trigger', label: 'Trigger'},
                    ]"
                    :items="[
                        {form: 'v-model', props_updated: 'modelValue', trigger: 'update:modelValue'},
                        {form: 'v-model:current-page', props_updated: 'currentPage', trigger: 'update:currentPage'},
                    ]"
                >
                </ph-data-table>
            </ph-card>
            <ph-card class="mb-3">
                <h5 class="fw-bold">Shared conventions</h5>
                <ph-data-table
                    :columns="[
                        {key: 'token', label: 'Token'},
                        {key: 'value', label: 'Value'},
                    ]"
                    :items="[
                        {token: 'none', value: '0'},
                        {token: 'xs', value: '0.25rem'},
                        {token: 'sm', value: '0.5rem'},
                        {token: 'md', value: '0.75rem'},
                        {token: 'lg', value: '1rem'},
                        {token: 'xl', value: '1.5rem'},
                        {token: '2xl', value: '2rem'},
                    ]"
                >
                </ph-data-table>

                <p>
                    Numeric values are interpreted as <strong>pixels</strong>. An unknown string is
                    passed through as a raw CSS value (e.g. <code>gap="1.25rem"</code>).
                </p>
                <p>
                    <strong>Variants.</strong> Components that read <code>variant</code> map the neutral/error names onto Bootstrap
                    classes: <code>error</code> → <code>bg-danger/alert-danger</code>, <code>neutral</code> → <code>text-bg-secondary</code>, and so on.
                    Valid values are enumerated per component below.
                </p>

                <p>
                    <strong>Slots.</strong> Where a component has both a <code>label</code> prop and a default slot, the slot wins when present.
                </p>

            </ph-card>

        </template>
    </ph-card>
</template>
<script>
export default {
    name: "PhuiOverview",
    data() {
        return {
            snippet1_1: `<ph-button variant="primary" @click="save">Save</ph-button>
<ph-input v-model="email" label="Email" />`,
            snippet1_1_1: `<php>
return [
    'title' => 'My Page',
    'styles' => ['/assets/app/styles/main.css', '/assets/app/styles/custom.css'],
    'state' => [...],
];
</php>
<template>
<div>My component content</div>
</template>`,
        }
    }
}
</script>